    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78839f99cae8c2019a304080570efd&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Adjunct Faculty - Undergraduate Studies Watertown Location: Watertown, SD Job Id: 223 # of Openings: 1 Position Information Mount Marty University, a Catholic and Benedictine institution in the Liberal Arts tradition, seeks applications on a continuous basis for a pool of qualified adjunct faculty to teach on our Watertown, SD campus. The number of positions varies each semester, depending upon the needs of the University. Hiring units will consult the adjunct pool when there is a need. Teaching assignments may include day, evening, blended, and online campus courses. Appointments may be renewable based on need, funding, and performance. High need courses include Theology and Philosophy. Salary: $745 per credit hour. Required Qualifications Minimum Higher Learning Commission requirements for qualified faculty: either a Master's degree in the area of specialization (content), or a Master's degree outside the area of specialization with 18 graduate credit hours in the area of specialization. Those interested must also be willing to support the mission of Mount Marty University and its Catholic and Benedictine values. Application Instructions To apply, please submit your CV and transcripts. More detailed information about the university, including the mission statement, can be found at http://www.mountmarty.edu. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a19de07068019dfdf83c2b5493&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Athletic Trainer Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 302 # of Openings: 1 This is a full time, exempt position that must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Handbook. In collaboration with the team physician, the Athletic Trainer provides preventative care, emergency care, clinical diagnosis, therapeutic intervention, and rehabilitation of injuries and medical conditions for Mount Marty’s intercollegiate athletic programs. This role serves as a vital communication link between the athlete, physician, coach, and family to determine the best route of treatment and return-to-play timeline. Mission To provide athletes with, and educate both athletes and coaches about, the care and prevention of athletic injuries. Duties and Responsibilities Clinical Care & Rehabilitation Coordinate the prevention, care, evaluation, and rehabilitation of injuries for varsity and junior varsity athletes Perform primary and secondary surveys or evaluations of all athletic-related injuries Responsible for taping, bracing, and padding of athletic-related injuries Deliver appropriate therapeutic modalities and distribute protocols for therapeutic exercise and rehabilitation Monitor ABC’s, CPR, First Aid, and other critical interventions during injury assessments Manage necessary referrals of musculoskeletal and other injuries to the appropriate medical provider and coordinate student-athlete appointments Work under the direction of the Team Physician to provide “medical clearance” for all injured student-athletes Administrative and Operations Direct and supervise the daily operation of the athletic training room and coordinate work-study students Maintain and protect health, insurance, injury, and other necessary records (via Sportsware) ensuring strict confidentiality and compliance Assist in developing the training room budget and initiating the purchase of supplies and equipment Implement and coordinate emergency action plans for all athletic venues Maintain administrative records including injury reports, treatments, and insurance documentation Communication and Support Provide medical coverage before, during, and after games/events; responsible for game/event preparation (ice, water, med kits, biohazard receptacles) Consult, advise, and cooperate with coaches and athletes regarding wellness decisions and injury status Assist in the organization and coordination of community education programs in sports medicine, fitness, and wellness Maintain state licensure and national certification by completing necessary CEUs and required CPR/AED/First Aid certifications Perform other duties as assigned by the Athletic Director and Head Athletic Trainer Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training required; Master’s degree in Athletic Training or related field from a CAATE accredited program preferred Experience: Two (2) years of post-graduate experience in the athletic training field (or equivalent) preferred Certifications & Licensure: ​BOC Certified Athletic Trainer in good standing Current South Dakota State licensure (or eligible to obtain) Current CPR/AED/First Aid for the Professional Rescuer or Basic Life Support for Healthcare Providers Commitment: Demonstrated commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University Physical Requirements and Working Conditions Schedule Adaptability: Must demonstrate extreme flexibility; the schedule is subject to frequent, last-minute changes due to weather, travel, and post-season play. The position requires nights, weekends, and holidays. Physical Demands: Ability to stand, walk, and sit for extended periods. Must be able to lift and carry up to 50 pounds (coolers, kits, equipment) and occasionally up to 100 pounds. Environmental Exposure: Frequent exposure to outdoor weather conditions and responsibility for monitoring environmental safety for athletes. Travel: Ability to travel with athletic teams for away competitions as assigned. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7883ac995981c201995e1d723c3214&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Bus Driver - Part-Time Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 216 # of Openings: 1 Bus Driver Mount Marty University is looking for part-time bus drivers to provide transportation for members of our athletic teams and students. All candidates must have or be able to receive a Class C Commercial Drivers License, from the State of South Dakota or State of their residence. Some overnight travel may be required. The ideal candidate must be committed in principle and practice to Mount Marty University’s mission as a Catholic and Benedictine university rooted in the Liberal Arts. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition.  The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants for this position must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references.  These materials will be submitted online to Careers at Mount Marty. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78879e9e46f5fc019e4bc789ad3265&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Track & Field Graduate Assistant Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 315 # of Openings: 1 Academic Requirements To be considered for this position, you must be accepted into the Mount Marty University Masters of Education Coaching Leadership Program. In order to be considered for the Master’s Program, you must have a 2.75 GPA, three letters of reference from a supervisor, coach, professor/colleague, and a 1-2-page essay explaining your purpose, goals, and commitment to this coaching program. Interested applicants can apply here. Compensation Candidate will receive a 2/3 tuition waiver from Mount Marty’s Master of Education in Coaching Leadership Program and $2,500 academic stipend. Additional income opportunities will be available during the off-season. Mount Marty Athletics Athletics is responsible for operations of all athletics teams, meeting the requirements of National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC) regulations. Mount Marty University Athletic Department, in accordance with the mission of the university, seeks to provide all students a variety of experiences which will promote and exemplify excellence in sportsmanship and athletic performance, enhance their education, prepare them for service to the human community, and provide a unique view of the university. The Athletic Department strives to provide the following services to the student-athlete: Enhance their education and educational opportunities. Develop character building. Positive and enjoyable experience. Appreciate giving back to the community through service. The Athletic Department strives to provide the following services to the university: Assist in the recruitment of new students. Assist in the fund raising efforts of the university. Assist in the visibility and public relations efforts of the university Essential Duties Assist with the development and implementation of training plans for designated event group(s) during indoor and outdoor track & field seasons.  Ideally, we are looking for someone who has high jump, long jump, and triple jump experience and/or experience with discus, shot put, javelin, weight throw, and hammer throw Coach student-athletes as assigned during practices and meets. Provide oversight and evaluation of student-athletes’ daily progress Recruit prospective student athletes in compliance with University-developed goals and within NAIA guidelines. Recruitment may include making initial contact with prospective students and families, assisting with campus visits, and maintaining regular contact with recruits May participate in event scheduling, budget management, procurement of equipment, all aspects of meet management for collegiate and high school events, and fundraising The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably-related duties Application Instructions Applicants must submit materials online at Careers at Mount Marty. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78839f9de0710c019e1d2a2e4601ea&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Staff Accountant Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 307 # of Openings: 1 This is a non-exempt full-time position and must adhere to the Mount Marty University handbook(s). The Staff Accountant provides essential support for the University's accounting functions. The Staff Accountant will work closely with the VP for Finance regarding university accounting, including journal entries, reconciliations, and audit preparation. Duties and Responsibilities System Administration ​ Assist in the administration of Anthology Finance by learning to configure financial codes, supporting the maintenance of the chart of accounts, and assisting with user security Financial Reporting ​ Prepare materials for annual Financial Statement and Financial Aid Single Audit Gather information for annual reporting and tax filings, including 990, IPEDs, and other federally required reports Prepare and process accurate and timely invoices for federal, state, and private grants by compiling all necessary supporting documentation to ensure expenditures align with grantor guidelines and University policy Serve as a primary point of contact for the campus community regarding budget-to-actual inquiries Financial Reconciliation ​ Collaborate with Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, and Payroll to ensure accurate and timely monthly close and reconciliation processes Maintain Fixed Asset & Depreciation schedules and balance sheet reconciliations Coordinate with the Financial Aid office on all Business Office transactions, including drawing federal funds and reconciling aid disbursements Other Duties ​ File sales and quarterly payroll reports timely Participate in special projects as assigned Perform additional duties as assigned by the Vice President for Finance and Administration Required Skills and Competencies Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and Word; Anthology Finance preferred Demonstrated customer service, multitasking, and confidentiality management skills Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in accounting Relevant accounting experience Commitment to the mission and values of Mount Marty University About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78859f9fd3baa0019ff150c0d4680c&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Learning Technology Support Specialist Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 323 # of Openings: 1 This is a full-time position and must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Employee Handbook. The Learning Technology Support Specialist provides support for technology used by faculty and students to further the mission of Mount Marty University. Mission: To assist the Information Technology Department in supporting the Universities learning technology needs. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide learning management system support for faculty and students. Assist faculty with the creation of static and video content for traditional, hybrid and distance learning classes. Research advances in educational technology and make recommendations for implementation at Mount Marty University. Serve as the primary point of contact for faculty for computer hardware and software. Facilitate the improvement, repair, and maintenance of lab and classroom technology. Create and provide training programs for students, faculty and staff on new and existing technology. Maintain an accurate inventory of learning technology used across campus. Maintain and improve training documents provided by ITSS and vendors. Work with ITSS team to provide an IT infrastructure that can support existing and new technology initiatives. Provide technology support and training to visitors using campus resources. Support and improve distance learning capabilities. Responsible for set-up and support of audio/visuals needs including live streams during on-campus events. Additional duties as assigned by VP of Technology. Qualifications: Associate or Bachelor Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Familiarity with learning management systems. Ability to communicate effectively across a variety of platforms. Comfortable speaking in front of large groups. Demonstrated technical and customer services skills. Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University. About MMU: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Process: Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b01a01f684da36ea2&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Facilities Technician III - Groundskeeper Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 325 # of Openings: 1 This is a non-exempt, full-time position and must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Employee Handbook. The Mount Marty University Facilities Tech III Groundskeeper position is responsible for the overall maintenance, upkeep, and aesthetic appearance of the grounds and outdoor areas of the Mount Marty University campus. This includes landscaping, turf management, tree and shrub care, hardscape maintenance, and seasonal tasks such as snow removal and leaf cleanup. The Groundskeeper plays a vital role in ensuring a safe, clean, and welcoming environment for employees, visitors, and the public. Mission: We strive to maintain a high quality of service in a timely manner. We do this by providing quality support through effective and experienced management. By supporting MMU, the facilities department is committed to establish and maintain a safe, clean, attractive and effective physical environment for the campus community, as well as to provide high quality support in a cost-effective manner. Key Responsibilities: Turf Management: ​ Mow, trim, and edge lawns and turf areas using a variety of equipment (mowers, trimmers, edgers). Apply fertilizer, pesticides, and herbicides in accordance with safety guidelines and regulations. Oversee irrigation systems, including monitoring, adjusting, and repairing sprinkler heads and lines, and winterizing sprinkler systems. Aerating, seeding, and sodding as needed to maintain healthy and lush turf. Landscaping and Horticulture: ​ Plant, cultivate, and maintain flower beds, shrubs, trees, and other plant life. Prune and trim trees and shrubs to promote healthy growth and maintain a neat appearance. Remove weeds and debris from landscaped areas. Mulch beds and around trees and shrubs. Hardscape and General Maintenance: ​ Maintain and repair walkways, paths, and parking lot surfaces. Clean and maintain outdoor furniture, benches, and other fixtures. Empty trash receptacles and manage recycling in outdoor areas. Pick up litter and debris to ensure the grounds are free of trash. Seasonal Tasks: ​Fall: Rake and blow leaves, and prepare grounds for winter. Winter: Perform snow and ice removal from walkways, entrances, and parking lots using shovels, snow blowers, and snowplows. Apply de-icing agents as needed to ensure safety. Spring: Prepare grounds for the growing season, including cleaning up winter debris, aerating, planting and watering. Equipment Operation and Maintenance: ​ Operate and maintain a variety of groundskeeping and shop equipment, including mowers (riding and push), tractors, trimmers, edgers, blowers, chainsaws, snow blowers, and plows. Perform routine maintenance on equipment and MMU fleet vehicles such as checking fluids, sharpening blades, and cleaning. Report any equipment malfunctions or maintenance needs to the supervisor. Schedule fleet vehicle maintenance, repairs, and inspections. Safety and Compliance: ​ Adhere to all safety protocols and use personal protective equipment (PPE) as required. Store and handle chemicals and fuels safely and in compliance with regulations. Maintain a clean and organized work area. Identify and report any safety hazards on the grounds. Other Duties as assigned: ​ Be available for 24 hour ON-CALL basis, some night and weekend work. Work Overtime as required in campus emergencies, severe weather conditions, and special events. Complete work orders for your area to standard. Maintain proper records for your area, fill out work orders, conduct inventories of parts on hand, order parts needed, complete any specific reports for equipment in your area. Perform preventative maintenance and implement new PM’s to extend life cycle of assets, asset reliability, and reduce operational expenses. Supervise, train, and support student employees assigned to your area. Perform event set ups and office furniture moves. May perform all duties of a Facility Technician 1 and 2. Assist facilities staff or other tasks assigned by Director of Operations or Director of Facilities and Maintenance. Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent 1-3 years of experience in groundskeeping, landscaping, or a related field Valid drivers license Knowledge and Skills: ​ Knowledge of plants, turf, and tree care best practices. Ability to safely operate and perform basic maintenance on groundskeeping equipment. Knowledge of safe chemical handling and application. Familiarity with snow and ice removal techniques. Strong attention to detail and a high standard for quality work. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Physical Requirements: ​ Ability to stand, walk, bend, stoop, and lift for extended periods. Ability to lift and carry up to 100 pounds. Willingness to work outdoors in various weather conditions (heat, cold, rain, snow). Ability to perform physically demanding tasks. Other: ​ Commercial fertilizer/herbicide applicator's license must be obtained. Commitment to the Mission of Mount Marty University. About MMU: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Process: Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a8a03fc2be01a0585919b81a40&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Facility Technician I Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 327 # of Openings: 1 This is a non-exempt, full-time position and must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Handbooks. The Facility Technician I cleans and maintains facilities/grounds to enhance the appearance of the buildings. Mission : The facilities department is committed to establishing and maintaining a safe, clean, attractive and effective physical environment for the campus community, as well as to provide high quality service and support in a cost-effective and timely manner. Duties and Responsibilities: Performs a variety of cleaning to ensure sanitary conditions are met to a level that floors and base molding shine and/or are bright and clean; colors are fresh, no buildup in corners or along walls, all vertical and horizontal surfaces have a freshly cleaned or polished appearance and have no accumulation of dust, dirt, marks, streaks, smudges, or fingerprints, lights all work and fixtures are clean, washroom and shower fixtures and tile gleam and are odor free, supplies are adequate, trash containers are clean and odor free Scrubs, mops, waxes and polishes floors using dry and wet mops, wax applicators, buffers, and floor machines Perform basic routine and preventive maintenance on facilities such as re-lamping fixtures, snow removal, ceiling tile replacement, painting, clearing drains, and general repairs Moves and arranges furniture Conduct work in a safe, productive, and environmentally friendly manner Be familiar and comply with the safety regulations and use safety equipment which apply to tools and chemicals you work wit h 7:00-3:30, and some night and weekend work Work overtime as required in campus emergencies, severe weather conditions and special events Supervise, train and support student employees assigned to you Maintain a friendly atmosphere within the department and the campus community Perform other duties as assigned by Associate Vice President of Facilities and Auxiliary Services and Director of Facilities Operations Perform the following tasks at the beginning of the work shift, before/after all breaks, at the end of the work shift, and frequently throughout the work shift; check/respond to email and submit/update scheduled (CMMS) tasks Ability to learn, and use computerized technology to communicate, monitor campus systems, and record keeping per department procedures Perform basic maintenance and operation of equipment; including saws, drills, routers and other miscellaneous tools to complete assigned maintenance tasks Perform basic installation/application of finishes, including caulking, painting, staining, and coatings Work to maintain shop cleanliness and that it is up to standards Communicate effectively and professionally with the public, staff, and students Support graduation ceremonies and other special events Snow removal as needed Qualifications: A High school diploma/GED or equivalent experience Ability to lift objects weighing up to 75 lbs and work off of ladders Valid driver’s license Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University Scope of Work: This is basic work in a wide variety of cleaning, maintenance and repair of campus buildings, facilities and grounds.  A general knowledge of all disciplines is required.  Performs varied tasks such as primary responsibility for routine, cleaning, maintenance, repair of facilities. Application Process Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three references through the online application system. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition.  The University has been noted regionally for its strong nursing programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. More detailed information about Mount Marty University including the mission statement, can be found at http://www.mountmarty.edu Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887ac9e2359d7019e46e7384b2d5d&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Campus Safety Officer - Part-time Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 311 # of Openings: 1 Position Overview Mount Marty University invites applications for a Campus Safety Officer (CSO). This is a part-time, non-benefits eligible position that must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Employee Handbook. Campus Safety Officers ( C SO) will assist in providing safety to  individuals on campus property and maintaining the security of campus buildings, facilities, parking lots, walkways, and grounds of the University. C SOs provide escort services and other safety services as needed and perform routine security and public safety patrol duties to maintain a safe environment for Mount Marty University and Sacred Heart Monastery. Officers must remain alert to all unusual activity especially emergency situations and provide first-line response, emergency management and/or referral if necessary. Qualifications CSOs must be able to stand and walk for long periods of time and operate security systems; the duties assigned are completed by foot patrol. Must have a valid driver's license. This is a night shift position. Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University. Applicants are required to pass a standard background check. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition.  The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants for this position must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references.  These materials will be submitted online to Careers at Mount Marty . Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/SubmitResume.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&source=&submissionClicked=true&fromAggregate=false&id=8a7883b58ab512a5018abcf49a1e16c1&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Wowsa! That file is huge! Sorry, but that just isn't going to work. Resume Submission Thank you for your interest. Please complete the fields below and click \"Submit\". Apply with a Resume Upload a text, word or pdf file by clicking a link below, or drag and drop into this box. Choose a File Google Drive Dropbox Uploading... remove Fax Number Please take a few minutes to fill out our application form. Required Fields are denoted with a \" \". Personal Information Clear All Fields First Name Preferred Name Last Name Email Attachments Resume Choose a file to upload remove Contact Information Mobile Phone Address City State Postal Code Comments Because we do business with the US Government, we must reach out to, hire and provide equal opportunity to qualified individuals. To help us measure how we are doing, in the following screens we are going to ask you to provide us with information about your race, gender, veteran status and if you have, or have had, a disability. As part of this procedure we are going to invite you to complete the following: Voluntary Self Identification of Gender, Ethnicity/Race Voluntary Self Identification of Veteran Status Voluntary Self Identification of Disability Any answers you give will be kept private and will not be used against you in any way. You are not required to disclose any of this information and completion of the questionnaires is entirely voluntary. Once you have completed this process, you will be directed to our application. Invitation to Self-Identify Gender, Ethnicity/Race Mount Marty University is subject to certain governmental recordkeeping and reporting requirements for the administration of civil rights laws and regulations. In order to comply with these laws, we invite applicants and employees to voluntarily self-identify their gender, race and ethnicity. Submission of this information is strictly voluntary and refusal to provide it will not subject you to any adverse treatment. The information obtained will be kept confidential and may only be used in accordance with the provision of applicable laws, executive orders, and regulations, including those that require the information to be summarized and reported to the federal government for civil rights enforcement. When reported, data will not identify any specific individual. This information will be maintained separately from your application for employment. If you do not wish to self-identify at this time, you may do so in the future  by submitting this form. Failure to provide the following information will not subject you to any adverse action or treatment. Mount Marty University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer. We provide equal employment opportunities to all qualified employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, religion, sex, age, marital status, national origin, sexual orientation, citizenship status, veteran status, disability or any other legally protected status. We prohibit discrimination in decisions concerning recruitment, hiring, compensation, benefits, training, termination, promotions, or any other condition of employment or career development. Gender: Male Female I decline to identify Ethnicity/Race: Hispanic or Latino A person of Cuban, Mexican, Puerto Rican, South or Central American, or other Spanish culture or origin regardless of race. White (Not Hispanic or Latino) A person having origins in any of the original peoples of Europe, the Middle East, or North Africa. Black or African American (Not Hispanic or Latino) A person having origins in any of the black racial groups of Africa. Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander (Not Hispanic or Latino) A person having origins in any of the peoples of Hawaii, Guam, Samoa, or other Pacific Islands. Asian (Not Hispanic or Latino) A person having origins in any of the original peoples of the Far East, Southeast Asia, or the Indian Subcontinent, including, for example, Cambodia, China, India, Japan, Korea, Malaysia, Pakistan, the Philippine Islands, Thailand, and Vietnam. American Indian or Alaska Native (Not Hispanic or Latino) A person having origins in any of the original peoples of North and South America (including Central America), and who maintains tribal affiliation or community attachment. Two or More Races (Not Hispanic or Latino) All persons who identify with more than one of the above five races. I decline to identify Invitation to Self-Identify Protected Veteran Status Mount Marty University is a Government contractor subject to the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974, as amended by the Jobs for Veterans Act of 2002, 38 U.S.C. 4212 (VEVRAA), which requires Government contractors to take affirmative action to employ and advance in employment: (1) disabled veterans; (2) recently separated veterans; (3) active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans; and (4) Armed Forces service medal veterans.\nThese classifications are defined as follows: A \"disabled veteran\" is one of the following: A veteran of the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service who is entitled to compensation (or who but for the receipt of military retired pay would be entitled to compensation) under laws administered by the Secretary of Veterans Affairs; or A person who was discharged or released from active duty because of a service-connected disability. A \"recently separated veteran\" means any veteran during the three-year period beginning on the date of such veteran's discharge or release from active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval, or air service. An \"active duty wartime or campaign badge veteran\" means a veteran who served on active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service during a war, or in a campaign or expedition for which a campaign badge has been authorized under the laws administered by the Department of Defense. An \"Armed forces service medal veteran\" means a veteran who, while serving on active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service, participated in a United States military operation for which an Armed Forces service medal was awarded pursuant to Executive Order 12985. Protected veterans may have additional rights under USERRA - the Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act. In particular, if you were absent from employment in order to perform service in the uniformed service, you may be entitled to be reemployed by your employer in the position you would have obtained with reasonable certainty if not for the absence due to service. For more information, call the U.S. Department of Labor's Veterans Employment and Training Service (VETS), toll-free, at 1-866-4-USA-DOL. If you believe you belong to any of the categories of protected veterans listed above, please indicate by checking the appropriate box below. As a Government contractor subject to VEVRAA, we request this information in order to measure the effectiveness of the outreach and positive recruitment efforts we undertake pursuant to VEVRAA. Submission of this information is voluntary and refusal to provide it will not subject you to any adverse treatment. The information provided will be used only in ways that are not inconsistent with the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974, as amended. The information you submit will be kept confidential, except that (i) supervisors and managers may be informed regarding restrictions on the work or duties of disabled veterans, and regarding necessary accommodations; (ii) first aid and safety personnel may be informed, when and to the extent appropriate, if you have a condition that might require emergency treatment; and (iii) Government officials engaged in enforcing laws administered by OFCCP, or enforcing the Americans with Disabilities Act, may be informed. I IDENTIFY AS ONE OR MORE OF THE CLASSIFICATIONS OF PROTECTED VETERAN LISTED ABOVE I AM NOT A PROTECTED VETERAN I DO NOT WISH TO IDENTIFY AT THIS TIME Privacy Policy Acknowledgement By checking this box, you acknowledge and consent to terms of the privacy policy which applies to the applicant tracking service being offered by Paycor on behalf of Mount Marty University. The privacy policy offers an explanation of how and why your data will be collected, how it will be used and disclosed, how it will be retained and secured, and what legal rights are associated with that data (including the rights of access, correction, and deletion). The policy also describes legal and contractual limitations on these rights. The specific rights and obligations of individuals living and working in different areas may vary by jurisdiction. Acceptance I have read and agree to this statement Submit powered by You've already applied! It looks like you've already applied to this job. You can still apply to our other openings, so why not check out our job list to see if there's something of interest. Seeing this message in error? Let us know by writing to jaymie.bloch@mountmarty.edu . GO TO JOB LIST CANCEL Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/SubmitResume.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&source=&submissionClicked=true&fromAggregate=false&id=8a7883b58ab512a5018abcf49a1e16c1&lang=es": {
      "title": "Mount Marty University",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Wowsa! That file is huge! Sorry, but that just isn't going to work. Resume Submission Gracias por su interés. Por favor responda lo siguiente y haga clic en \"Solicitar\". Cargar r﻿ésum﻿é Cargar un archivo text, word o pdf haciendo clic en alguna de las ligas de abajo, o arrastre o eliga en esta caja. Escoga un documento Google Drive Dropbox Subiendo... borrar Fax Number Please take a few minutes to fill out our application form. Required Fields are denoted with a \" \". Datos personales Borrar toda la informaci﻿ón Nombre Nombre que prefiere Apellido(s) Correo Electr﻿ónico Anexos Escoga un documento para subir borrar Informaci﻿ón para contactarlo Tel﻿éfono Celular Direcci﻿ón Ciudad Estado C﻿ódigo Postal Comentarios Como deber a nuestra empresa y a el Gobierno Federal de los Estado Unidos, nuestra empresa ofrece oportunidades equitativas de empleo a aquellos candidatos calificados. Para conllevar una contrataci﻿ón justa, a continuaci﻿ón se le preguntar﻿á sobre su raza, g﻿énero, estatus militar y si ha tenido o tiene alguna discapacidad m﻿édica. Como parte de este procedimiento le invitamos a completar lo siguiente: Auto-Identificaci﻿ón Voluntaria de G﻿énero, Etnicidad/Raza Auto-Identificaci﻿ón Voluntaria de Estatus Militar Declaraci﻿ón voluntaria de discapacidad Cada una de las respuestas ser﻿á privada y de ninguna manera se utilizar﻿án en su contra. Este cuestionario es completamente voluntario, no es requerido revelar esta informaci﻿ón. Una vez completado el proceso, usted ver﻿á el formulario de solicitud. Invitaci﻿ón a Auto-Identificar el G﻿énero y la Etnicidad/Raza Mount Marty University se somete a requisitos gubernamentales de mantenimiento de registros e informes para la administraci﻿ón de regulaciones y leyes de derechos civiles. Para concordar con estas regulaciones, invitamos a los candidatos y empleados a auto-identificarse voluntariamente sobre su g﻿énero, raza y etnicidad. No es requerido revelar esta informaci﻿ón y la falta de esta informaci﻿ón no har﻿á que tenga/reciba un trato diferente. La informaci﻿ón recopilada es confidencial y solo se puede usar en conformidad con las leyes aplicables, ﻿órdenes ejecutivas, y normas, incluyendo aquellos que requieren que esta informaci﻿ón sea resumida y entregada al gobierno federal para la pr﻿áctica de derechos civiles. Al entregar esta informaci﻿ón, no habr﻿á ninguna asociaci﻿ón con un individuo en espec﻿Ífico. Esta informaci﻿ón ser﻿á guardada aparte de su solicitud laboral. Si no desea identificarse en este momento, usted podr﻿á hacerlo en el futuro usando este formulario. El no compartir esta informaci﻿ón no le causar﻿á alguna adversidad. Mount Marty University es un proveedor y empleador que ofrece oportunidades equitativas de empleo para todos aquellos empleados y candidatos calificados sin importar raza, religi﻿ón, sexo, edad, estado civil, origen nacional, orientaci﻿ón sexual, nacionalidad, estatus militar, discapacidad o cualquier otro estatus protegido. Prohibimos la discriminaci﻿ón al tomar decisiones en cuanto a contratar, compensaci﻿ón, beneficios, entrenamiento, terminaci﻿ón de contrato, promoci﻿ón/ascenso, o cualquier otra condici﻿ón de empleo o desarrollo profesional. G﻿énero: Masculino Femenino No deseo contestar Etnicidad/Raza: Hispano o Latino Personas de origen cubano, mexicano, puertorrique﻿ño, de Suram﻿érica, Centroam﻿érica o de cualquier otra cultura espa﻿ñola u origen espa﻿ñol, independientemente de su raza. Blanco (No Hispano o Latino) Personas que descienden de cualquiera de los habitantes originales de Europa, el Medio Oriente, o el Norte de ﻿África. Negro o Afro-americano (No Hispano o Latino) Personas que descienden de cualquiera de los grupos raciales negros de ﻿África. Nativo de Hawai o de otra de las Islas del Pac﻿ífico (No Hispano o Latino) Personas que descienden de los habitantes originales de Hawai, Guam, Samoa u otras islas del Pac﻿ífico. Asi﻿ático (No Hispano o Latino) Son las personas que descienden de los habitantes originales del Lejano Oriente, el sureste asi﻿ático o el subcontinente Indio, por ejemplo: Cambodia, China, India, Jap﻿ón, Corea, Malasia, Pakist﻿án, Las Islas Filipinas, Tailandia y Vietnam. Indio Americano o Nativo de Alaska (No Hispano o Latino) Son las personas que descienden de los habitantes originales de Norte y Sur de Am﻿érica (incluyendo Centroam﻿érica) y quienes mantienen una afiliaci﻿ón tribal o una relaci﻿ón comunitaria. Dos o mas Razas (No Hispano o Latino) Todas las personas que identifican con m﻿ás de una de las cinco razas anteriores. No deseo contestar Invitaci﻿ón a Auto-Identificar el Estatus Militar Mount Marty University es un contratista gubernamental que est﻿á sujeto al Acto de \"Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance\" de 1974, modificado por el Acto de \"Jobs for Veterans\" del 2002, 38 U.S.C. 4212 (VEVRAA), que exige a los contratistas gubernamentales tomar medidas positivas para contratar y avanzar con los empleos. (1) veteranos discapacitados; (2) veteranos reci﻿én retirados; (3) veteranos en servicio activo de guerra o de campaign badge ; y (4) veteranos condecorados en las Fuerzas Armadas\".\nEstos grupos se definen a continuaci﻿ón: Un \"veterano discapacitado\" se refiere a lo siguiente: Un veterano discapacitado de los Estados Unidos es quien haya prestado servicio en el ej﻿ército, marina,o fuerza a﻿érea que tiene derecho a una indemnizaci﻿ón (u otra persona que tiene este derecho de jubilaci﻿ón pagada) seg﻿ún las leyes administradas por el Secretario de Asuntos Veteranos; o Un soldado retirado del servicio activo con relaci﻿ón a una discapacidad adquirida durante el servicio. Un \"veterano reci﻿én retirado\" se refiere a cualquier veterano durante el periodo de tres a﻿ños que empieza justo despu﻿és de salir del servicio activo en el ej﻿ército, marina, o fuerza a﻿érea estadounidense. Un \"veterano en servicio activo de guerra o de campaign badge \" se refiere a una persona que prest﻿ó servicio en el ej﻿ército, marina o fuerza a﻿érea estadounidense durante una guerra, o una operaci﻿ón de campa﻿ña la cual ha sido autorizada seg﻿ún las leyes administradas por el Departamento de Defensa. Un \"veterano condecorado del servicio de las Fuerzas Armadas\" se refiere a un veterano que, mientras estaba en servicio activo con el ej﻿ército, marina o fuerza a﻿érea estadounidense, particip﻿ó en una operaci﻿ón militar para los Estados Unidos donde le concedieron una medalla del Servicio de las Fuerza Armadas conforme al Executive Order 12985. Veteranos con un estatus protegido pueden tener derechos adicionales seg﻿ún \"USERRA - the Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act\". En particular, si dej﻿ó un empleo debido a prestar su servicio militar, es posible que tenga derecho a reintegrarse a la posici﻿ón y empresa anterior o a lo merecido si no hubiese sido por la ausencia del servicio militar. Para m﻿ás informaci﻿ón, llame al U.S. Department of Labor's Veterans Employment and Training Service (VETS), sin cargos, al 1-866-4-USA-DOL. Si usted cree que pertenece a uno de los grupos de veteranos protegidos mencionados anteriormente, por favor ind﻿Íquelo seleccionando la casilla correcta. Como un contratista gubernamental que est﻿á sujeto al VEVRAA, pedimos esta informaci﻿ón para analizar la efectividad de nuestro alcance y esfuerzo de contrataci﻿ón que asumimos conforme al VEVRAA. Esta informaci﻿ón no es requerida sino m﻿ás bien voluntaria. No ser﻿á perjudicado/a al no compartir esta informaci﻿ón. La informaci﻿ón que comparta ser﻿á utilizada solamente de manera consistente con el Acto modificado de \"Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance\" de 1974. La informaci﻿ón que recibamos ser﻿á confidencial, excepto (i) cuando los supervisores y gerentes tienen que ser informados sobre una restricci﻿ón en el trabajo o responsabilidades de veteranos discapacitados, y sobre alg﻿ún alojamiento necesario; (ii) cuando el personal de primeros auxilios y de seguridad tienen que ser informados de alguna condici﻿ón m﻿édica o que requiere una atenci﻿ón inmediata; y (iii) cuando los funcionarios gubernamentales encargados de aplicar leyes administradas por el OFCCP, o del Americans with Disabilities Act tienen que ser informados en general. ME IDENTIFICO COMO MIEMBRO DE UNO O M﻿ÁS DE LOS GRUPOS DE VETERANOS PROTEGIDOS MENCIONADOS NO SOY UN VETERANO PROTEGIDO NO DESEO CONTESTAR Reconocimiento de la Pol﻿ítica de Privacidad Al seleccionar la casilla anterior, usted reconoce y acepta los t﻿érminos de la pol﻿ítica de privacidad que aplican a los servicios de reclutamiento que ofrece Paycor en nombre de Mount Marty University. La pol﻿ítica de privacidad ofrece una explicaci﻿ón de como y por qu﻿é su informaci﻿ón ser﻿á recolectada, como ser﻿á usada y compartida, como ser﻿á guardada y asegurada, y los derechos legales asociados con la informaci﻿ón (incluyendo los derechos de acceso, correcci﻿ón y supresi﻿ón). La pol﻿ítica tambi﻿én describe las limitaciones legales y contractuales de estos derechos. Los derechos y obligaciones espec﻿íficos de los individuos pueden variar seg﻿ún la jurisdicci﻿ón en donde trabajen y vivan. Aceptaci﻿ón He le﻿ído y acepto esta declaraci﻿ón Solicitar powered by ﻿¡Usted ya solicit﻿ó este puesto! Parece que usted ya solicit﻿ó este puesto. Todav﻿ía puede solicitar otros puestos. Visite la lista de vacantes para ver si hay algo que le interese. ﻿¿Ve este mensaje por error? Escr﻿íbanos a jaymie.bloch@mountmarty.edu . IR A LISTA DE VACANTES CANCELAR Mount Marty University"
    }
